# arvo-mask-contracts. Design

The mask operations contract. One trait declaration:
`MaskOps<const W: Width>`. Concrete impls live in `arvo-bitmask`.
Consumers writing mask-generic code bind to this surface to keep
their transitive dependency footprint small. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.

Depends on `notko`, `arvo-storage`, `arvo-strategy` (for `Width`),
`arvo-bits-contracts`.

## MaskOps

```rust
pub const trait MaskOps<const W: Width>: Sized + Copy {
    fn empty() -> Self;
    fn full() -> Self;
    fn set(self, idx: USize) -> Self;
    fn clear(self, idx: USize) -> Self;
    fn test(self, idx: USize) -> Bool;
    fn count(self) -> USize;
    fn union(self, other: Self) -> Self;
    fn intersection(self, other: Self) -> Self;
    fn difference(self, other: Self) -> Self;
    fn complement(self) -> Self;
    fn mask_for_width(n: USize) -> Self;
}
```

`W` is the mask width (number of bits the mask covers), typed as
`Width` per the substrate's no-bare-primitives discipline.
Default-method bodies compose `BitLogic` from `arvo-bits-contracts`.
Concrete impls in `arvo-bitmask` supply the storage and may override
defaults with hardware-specific implementations.

`mask_for_width(n)` produces a mask with the lowest n bits set.
Consumed by `Narrow<T>` impls to truncate a wider raw to fit a typed
container; body composes through `BitPrim::mask_low(n)` from
arvo-bits-contracts.

## Naming

`arvo-bitmask::Mask<W>` is the concrete chassis struct (type-generic
over a Bits-shape word). `arvo-mask-contracts::MaskOps<const W:
Width>` is the abstract operation contract (const-generic over
width). Different shapes, different roles, different crates. The
distinct names eliminate the prior single-`Mask` clash that mixed
struct and trait under one name.

## Concrete impls in arvo-bitmask

```rust
impl const MaskOps<{ Width::from_u16(64) }>
    for Mask<Bits<64, Hot, Unsigned>>
{
    /* delegates to inherent surface on Mask<W> */
}

impl const MaskOps<{ Width::from_u16(256) }>
    for Mask<Bits<256, Hot, Unsigned>>
{
    /* same shape */
}
```

Round 202605031748 added these impls. The trait is no longer
stranded; consumers can bind generically on `T: MaskOps<{ width }>`
and reach the full operation set in const context.

